course: dictionary
lesson: 11132
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words and sentences around a word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. «The wicked witch» comes from a fairy tale, so wicked means very bad, evil or cruel.
explain: «A wicked grin» does not mean the grin is cruel. A grin is a smile, and a wicked grin is a playful, naughty smile, the kind someone has before a joke. The word around wicked gives the clue.
explain: In slang, especially in the UK, «That's wicked!» means excellent or brilliant. Ask yourself: is the speaker praising something or blaming someone? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
fact: Wicked means very bad, evil or cruel, as in «the wicked witch».
fact: Wicked can also mean naughty in a playful way, as in «a wicked grin» or «a wicked sense of humour».
fact: In UK slang, «That's wicked!» means excellent or brilliant.
fact: In New England, wicked can mean very.
fact: The same word can have a very different meaning, so always check the context before you decide.
exercise: «The wicked witch cast a spell on the castle.» What does wicked mean here? | Excellent and brilliant | Playful and naughty | *Very bad and cruel | Very quiet
exercise: The text says «a wicked grin». What does wicked mean here? | Very old | *Playful and a little naughty | Evil and cruel | Grey and damp
exercise: Jayden shouts «That's wicked!» after a goal. What does he mean? | *Brilliant, excellent | Very evil | Very wet | Very tired
test: Which meaning fits «a wicked sense of humour»? | Very old | Wet and grey | Very bad and cruel | *Playful and a little naughty
test: Ella reads «The wicked stepmother locked the door.» What does wicked mean? | Quiet | Playful | *Very cruel and bad | Excellent
exam: Which meaning fits «That's wicked, we won the match!»? | Naughty in a playful way | Very old | Very bad and cruel | *Excellent and brilliant, in slang
